WEBVTT

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:11.910
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:17.710
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.400
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:29.130
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.470
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:35.350
But, with you...

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.430
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:39.270 --> 00:00:43.020
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:47.740
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:52.120
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.700
Just to survive!

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:55.660
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:57.500
Take this moment...

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:01.120
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.330
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.330 --> 00:01:05.170
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:08.880
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:11.010
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.720
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.390
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.560
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:20.390
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.310
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:31.517 --> 00:01:35.754
Having joined DDS Class A's special
extra-curricular training…

00:01:35.954 --> 00:01:39.324
…we from Class Q are trying to
solve the unsolved case of…

00:01:39.491 --> 00:01:43.996
…Jack the Ripper's serial killings on the island
where the tragic event took place.

00:01:45.964 --> 00:01:52.638
However, what was waiting for us at the crime
scene was an actual brutal murder case.

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:58.844
Saburoumaru-san was found murdered and then
chopped in half in a double-door closed room.

00:02:00.179 --> 00:02:04.049
The next day, another Class A student,
Shishido Takeshi-san was…

00:02:04.316 --> 00:02:06.418
…found ruthlessly murdered.

00:02:07.986 --> 00:02:11.957
Jack the Ripper might be one of the 11 of us here!

00:02:12.591 --> 00:02:15.661
What do you think of him, Kyuu-kun?

00:02:16.562 --> 00:02:20.566
This is how Jack the Ripper created
the double-door closed room.

00:02:21.466 --> 00:02:22.734
Half a century ago…

00:02:22.968 --> 00:02:24.469
And two days ago.

00:02:25.437 --> 00:02:30.342
The mysterious genius Amakusa Ryuu-kun
solved the double-door closed room trick.

00:02:31.443 --> 00:02:36.615
And just when we and Ryuu-kun were coming
up with a theory about the second murder…

00:02:37.382 --> 00:02:39.318
…there was a third murder.

00:02:40.052 --> 00:02:43.188
We'll charge in to the room, you
in the lead, Touyama-kun!

00:02:44.756 --> 00:02:48.026
The victim was a member of Class
A, Gouda Kyousuke-san.

00:02:49.494 --> 00:02:53.765
It was a horrible case where three people
were murdered in a mere two day span.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:59.538
The fact that we were unable to escape the island
due to the harsh storm struck fear in us.

00:03:00.038 --> 00:03:04.843
But we, as detectives, hardened ourselves to
the cruelty in order to solve the mystery.

00:03:06.612 --> 00:03:11.216
Before each murder there three portraits were cut in a way that match each of the murders.

00:03:15.187 --> 00:03:18.724
If you want to re-inspect the crime scene,
use your body instead of a computer!

00:03:18.857 --> 00:03:19.691
Your body!

00:03:19.858 --> 00:03:21.827
Geez, you're annoying…

00:03:22.928 --> 00:03:27.366
Huh? Aren't these pictures too
low for you to see, Kinta?

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:31.737
What? Oh, come to think of it, they are displayed
lower than they would usually be.

00:03:32.104 --> 00:03:33.905
They're displayed at the perfect height for me…

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.208
Okay, I should input this, too.

00:03:40.245 --> 00:03:42.314
What's this smell?

00:03:51.089 --> 00:03:51.823
It's this.

00:03:54.126 --> 00:03:56.028
I've smelled this smell before somewhere…

00:03:59.431 --> 00:04:01.600
Oh, this pattern is…

00:04:03.669 --> 00:04:04.603
Hey, Kazuma!

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:06.505
Look at this pattern.

00:04:06.638 --> 00:04:08.707
Geez, how load can you be?

00:04:09.174 --> 00:04:10.175
Alright! Finished!

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:15.113
Eh? T-That's ridiculous!

00:04:16.715 --> 00:04:19.318
They're all dried up now.

00:04:20.419 --> 00:04:23.121
But the shape of the shoe is still quite clear.

00:04:23.789 --> 00:04:26.758
These footprints are much too distinct.

00:04:27.326 --> 00:04:32.931
It does seem these footprints were intentionally
made in order to lure you guys to the crime scene…

00:04:33.465 --> 00:04:36.735
Anyway, let's try reproducing the situation.

00:04:46.678 --> 00:04:48.113
A pink and white polka-dot patter…

00:04:49.815 --> 00:04:52.451
Didn't I tell you not to say the pattern out load?

00:04:55.153 --> 00:04:58.957
Oh, I'm sorry. Did it hurt that much?

00:05:00.726 --> 00:05:01.393
That's strange…

00:05:03.295 --> 00:05:06.198
This footprint is definitely strange!

00:05:10.936 --> 00:05:13.905
But I still can't believe that what
you're saying is true…

00:05:14.539 --> 00:05:19.544
Considering those footprints, there's only one
person that we can deduce to be the culprit!

00:05:19.911 --> 00:05:24.716
But when Gouda-san was murdered, the
culprit must have been in the room.

00:05:27.352 --> 00:05:30.055
We all saw it clearly from here.

00:05:30.856 --> 00:05:34.493
That's why we're going there now to solve that trick.

00:05:36.228 --> 00:05:39.865
At that time, we judged that the culprit
was still inside the room.

00:05:40.365 --> 00:05:43.435
We left you and Yukihina-san there and
the rest of us headed up to the room.

00:05:46.171 --> 00:05:47.105
This is it.

00:05:50.242 --> 00:05:51.376
Bloody footprints!

00:05:58.083 --> 00:06:00.552
The door to the crime scene seems to be locked.

00:06:09.094 --> 00:06:10.996
The next room also, eh?

00:06:12.097 --> 00:06:13.064
I guess it can't be helped.

00:06:13.965 --> 00:06:17.636
Let's try to remember the crime scene as we saw it.

00:06:17.936 --> 00:06:22.240
If only Megu and her photographic
memory were there at that time.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.311
That's it!

00:06:26.578 --> 00:06:28.547
W-What is it, you two?

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:31.616
There's something I want you to recollect, Megu.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.785
Okay. What is it?

00:06:34.419 --> 00:06:37.456
Try to remember the circumstances at
the time when we were looking up…

00:06:38.056 --> 00:06:41.426
…at the lighted room from outside, including
where everybody was standing at the time.

00:06:47.899 --> 00:06:49.100
It was like this.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.571
Just as I thought.

00:06:53.271 --> 00:06:55.140
His alibi is completely broken now.

00:06:55.407 --> 00:06:58.143
But, why did the culprit do this?

00:07:01.513 --> 00:07:02.547
A rat again!

00:07:02.848 --> 00:07:05.317
It's all right. They won't bite humans.

00:07:09.521 --> 00:07:10.355
That's it.

00:07:10.555 --> 00:07:11.656
I got it!

00:07:11.656 --> 00:07:15.594
Hey!

00:07:15.594 --> 00:07:17.295
Hey, this is a serious matter!

00:07:17.662 --> 00:07:19.331
Kinta. Kazuma.

00:07:19.498 --> 00:07:21.266
We know who the culprit is.

00:07:21.266 --> 00:07:22.701
Eh?

00:07:22.701 --> 00:07:24.035
Yeah. Us, too.

00:07:24.769 --> 00:07:25.904
The mystery has been solved!

00:07:30.008 --> 00:07:34.546
What in the world are you thinking, calling
us, even Dan-Sensei, out at this hour?

00:07:35.146 --> 00:07:37.983
It's okay. Let's listen to what they have to say.

00:07:37.983 --> 00:07:39.584
Eh?

00:07:39.584 --> 00:07:43.522
The look on their faces tells me that they
have grasped onto the truth of the case.

00:07:43.922 --> 00:07:45.657
Yes. That's exactly why.

00:07:46.024 --> 00:07:46.992
W-What did you say?

00:07:47.459 --> 00:07:49.294
We will reveal everything now.

00:07:49.828 --> 00:07:53.798
The truth of the case, and the
true identity of the culprit.

00:07:54.799 --> 00:07:55.967
There are five hints.

00:07:56.735 --> 00:08:00.672
One, the circumstances before Gouda-san's
corpse was found.

00:08:01.640 --> 00:08:03.842
Two, the abnormal footprints.

00:08:04.976 --> 00:08:08.246
Three, the condition that the half of
Saburoumaru-san's body was in.

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:11.416
Four, the handkerchief that was on the floor.

00:08:12.317 --> 00:08:15.053
And five, the positions of the three portraits.

00:08:16.087 --> 00:08:17.989
There's only one answer!

00:08:19.558 --> 00:08:26.197
Interesting. Then let's hear the truth about the
case that you guys claim to have solved.

00:08:26.598 --> 00:08:27.966
First of all, hint number one.

00:08:28.433 --> 00:08:30.468
The circumstances before Gouda-san's
corpse was found…

00:08:30.835 --> 00:08:36.174
This made us sure that the culprit is one of us here.

00:08:36.408 --> 00:08:37.509
Hold on a second!

00:08:38.043 --> 00:08:42.581
We were all watching the hand being dragged
in by somebody at that time!

00:08:44.049 --> 00:08:46.918
There's no way that the culprit could be one of us.

00:08:48.153 --> 00:08:50.121
That was exactly what the culprit was intending.

00:08:51.156 --> 00:08:55.026
The truth is that the culprit wasn't
in the room at the time.

00:08:55.493 --> 00:08:57.028
W-What did you say?

00:08:57.495 --> 00:09:00.298
Then, how do you explain the
hand getting dragged in?

00:09:01.032 --> 00:09:07.138
I will begin by explaining to you how
the culprit created that situation.

00:09:11.009 --> 00:09:14.546
The culprit tied a white string
around an amputated arm…

00:09:15.146 --> 00:09:18.783
And let it bang down through an opening
on the other side of the window like this.

00:09:20.085 --> 00:09:24.456
And then he pulled the string unnoticed
in the midst of the confusion.

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:30.161
This way it would seem as if the hand had been
dragged in by somebody in the room.

00:09:31.096 --> 00:09:31.997
How disappointing.

00:09:32.797 --> 00:09:34.366
You guys called us just for this?

00:09:35.467 --> 00:09:37.769
There's one big mistake in your reasoning.

00:09:38.503 --> 00:09:42.607
If what you said was true, Gouda's arm
should have been beside the window.

00:09:43.208 --> 00:09:47.512
But in actuality, Gouda's arms were
located far away from the window.

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.450
The hand that we saw on the window
wasn't Gouda-san's arm.

00:09:52.450 --> 00:09:54.185
Eh?

00:09:54.185 --> 00:10:00.592
The arm was that of the first victim, it was
Saburomaru-san's missing right arm.

00:10:02.193 --> 00:10:03.028
What did you say?

00:10:03.495 --> 00:10:08.233
This is the psychological trick that
Jack the Ripper constructed.

00:10:09.067 --> 00:10:13.471
We all headed for the crime scene after
we saw the hand being dragged in.

00:10:14.939 --> 00:10:20.078
The first thing we saw when we got there were
the bloody footprints that led to the room.

00:10:21.780 --> 00:10:25.583
Naturally, we thought that room
was the room with the lights on.

00:10:27.619 --> 00:10:30.722
But the room which had its lights on was actually…

00:10:31.122 --> 00:10:35.527
…not the room the footprints led
to, but the room next door.

00:10:37.796 --> 00:10:41.299
If I, the one with the photographic
memory, had been there…

00:10:41.633 --> 00:10:44.636
The unnaturalness of the scene
would have been obvious.

00:10:45.837 --> 00:10:49.307
The room where the hand was sticking out was
the fifth room counting from the right.

00:10:50.709 --> 00:10:54.079
But Gouda-san's corpse was found
in the room next door.

00:10:54.379 --> 00:10:56.147
The fourth room counting from the right.

00:10:57.315 --> 00:10:58.516
In other words, the culprit…

00:10:58.783 --> 00:11:02.120
…by using two rooms, made
us mistake the crime scene…

00:11:03.088 --> 00:11:04.823
…and seized his alibi.

00:11:05.256 --> 00:11:06.224
Oh, my!

00:11:06.691 --> 00:11:07.892
Why weren't we able to realize that?

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.996
Wait a minute! I understand the trick involved.

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:15.533
But you can't solve the case with just that!

00:11:16.034 --> 00:11:19.637
She's right! Do you know who the culprit is?

00:11:20.371 --> 00:11:20.972
Of course.

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:25.410
Just who is Jack the Ripper, the culprit of this case?

00:11:26.111 --> 00:11:28.413
The answer to that is given with hint number two.

00:11:28.947 --> 00:11:30.415
The abnormal footprints.

00:11:33.651 --> 00:11:37.222
Could you go up these stairs for us, Yukihira-san?

00:11:37.989 --> 00:11:41.593
Hey! Why don't you just say it?

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:45.363
I want you to verify what the culprit actually did.

00:11:45.697 --> 00:11:46.598
Please.

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:53.538
W-What is it?

00:11:53.605 --> 00:11:54.405
Please don't move.

00:11:55.707 --> 00:11:57.375
Please look at your feet from there.

00:12:02.013 --> 00:12:04.215
These footprints aren't right!

00:12:04.516 --> 00:12:05.116
That's right.

00:12:05.850 --> 00:12:07.085
It's obvious when you actually try.

00:12:07.485 --> 00:12:11.356
If the culprit had walked up these
steps in a normal manner…

00:12:11.756 --> 00:12:15.326
…the whole sole from the toe to the heel wouldn't
be left marked on these narrow steps.

00:12:16.394 --> 00:12:19.497
The correct footprints would have
been only half of the sole.

00:12:20.431 --> 00:12:23.134
Then, how did these footprints get here?

00:12:23.868 --> 00:12:26.571
These footprints weren't made while walking.

00:12:27.739 --> 00:12:33.545
The culprit left these shoe marks using his hands,
pressing a muddy shoe onto each step.

00:12:35.446 --> 00:12:36.381
But the culprit…

00:12:37.348 --> 00:12:41.319
…forgot how footprints would normally
be left when walking up the stairs.

00:12:42.287 --> 00:12:43.121
What do you mean?

00:12:43.655 --> 00:12:47.725
I mean there's only one answer
that these footprints lead to.

00:12:48.259 --> 00:12:50.161
isn't that right, Dan-Sensei?

00:12:51.462 --> 00:12:52.630
The true culprit…

00:12:53.231 --> 00:12:54.265
Jack the Ripper…

00:12:55.867 --> 00:12:56.801
…is you!

00:13:00.104 --> 00:13:03.107
That's the only way to think of it that makes sense.

00:13:03.608 --> 00:13:08.913
It was you who told me to stay behind when
Gouda-san was murdered, Dan-Sensei.

00:13:09.681 --> 00:13:16.888
That was because you thought that your trick might
be revealed if I went there with the others, right?

00:13:19.057 --> 00:13:21.326
Please answer, Dan-Sensei.

00:13:23.795 --> 00:13:25.530
What would be my motive?

00:13:27.298 --> 00:13:33.004
Just why would I have to kill my precious students?

00:13:35.173 --> 00:13:40.345
Well? If you can't answer that,
you can't make me the culprit.

00:13:42.046 --> 00:13:42.947
You see…

00:13:43.514 --> 00:13:45.550
Well? Answer me!

00:13:52.123 --> 00:13:52.790
Kazuma!

00:13:54.225 --> 00:13:56.694
Help! Kinta's been…

00:13:58.363 --> 00:14:00.732
Kinta's been murdered by Jack the Ripper!

00:14:16.181 --> 00:14:16.915
Kinta!

00:14:26.191 --> 00:14:27.292
What's this?

00:14:34.800 --> 00:14:35.901
Just kidding!

00:14:38.804 --> 00:14:42.241
This is your motive, Dan-Sensei.

00:14:42.674 --> 00:14:45.410
Geez. You really fooled us.

00:14:46.278 --> 00:14:47.713
Ups-a-daisy.

00:15:03.328 --> 00:15:05.697
Alright, wake up please!

00:15:07.733 --> 00:15:10.102
Huh? Where am I?

00:15:10.936 --> 00:15:13.972
None of them were truly dead to begin with.

00:15:14.673 --> 00:15:17.242
Man… We were all completely fooled by it.

00:15:17.476 --> 00:15:20.178
We would never expect that people
who were supposed to be dead…

00:15:20.479 --> 00:15:23.181
…were acting as the various parts
of the chopped up bodies.

00:15:23.582 --> 00:15:29.521
You made these holes that can fit different body
parts at various locations throughout the building.

00:15:30.222 --> 00:15:32.991
And made people of Class A act as the corpses.

00:15:35.827 --> 00:15:38.764
In the beginning, we were shocked
by the mutilated corpse…

00:15:39.064 --> 00:15:42.134
…and we weren't able to think that the
other half might be hidden, but…

00:15:42.234 --> 00:15:43.168
Of course we couldn't find it.

00:15:44.169 --> 00:15:48.707
The other half of Saburoumaru-san's
body was buried alive.

00:15:49.775 --> 00:15:54.112
Damn it! Why does a Tokyo University
student like me have to do this?

00:15:58.016 --> 00:16:01.353
But it would cause suspicion if only one
body part was missing each time

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:08.994
That's why you made each one of them act
as a body part for Shisido-san's murder.

00:16:13.832 --> 00:16:16.935
And in the case of Gouda-san's murder,
the head was that of Gouda-san, but…

00:16:17.302 --> 00:16:21.573
…the body was Shisido-san's and the
arms were Saburoumaru-san's.

00:16:22.908 --> 00:16:24.643
While searching through the building…

00:16:25.243 --> 00:16:28.213
I found these three supposedly dead people hiding.

00:16:28.614 --> 00:16:30.816
Although I felt a little sorry about
it since they were my seniors…

00:16:31.183 --> 00:16:36.421
…I knocked them out and made them
act out dead body parts once more.

00:16:37.055 --> 00:16:41.159
And then, using the gimmicks that
were left in Shishido-san's room…

00:16:41.393 --> 00:16:44.062
…we reproduced the crime. That's about it.

00:16:44.896 --> 00:16:47.733
The remaining two Class A members,
Yukihira-san and Shiramine-san.

00:16:48.133 --> 00:16:50.435
You two were in on it too, right?

00:16:51.003 --> 00:16:52.137
Ah… Yes.

00:16:52.771 --> 00:16:58.744
So the five people of Class A were here as
the cast for this case from the beginning.

00:16:59.378 --> 00:17:01.313
Isn't that right, Dan-Sensei?

00:17:07.552 --> 00:17:09.421
Isn't it?

00:17:15.394 --> 00:17:17.429
You win. You win.

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.865
That was well done, guys!

00:17:20.499 --> 00:17:21.299
Sensei!

00:17:23.869 --> 00:17:24.836
Damn!

00:17:25.671 --> 00:17:27.973
But can you tell me one thing?

00:17:28.240 --> 00:17:28.940
What is it?

00:17:29.408 --> 00:17:33.912
What caused you to think that nobody was dead?

00:17:34.446 --> 00:17:36.415
That is hint number three.

00:17:37.015 --> 00:17:38.850
The cut up Saburoumaru-san.

00:17:40.686 --> 00:17:44.423
The rats ate up the ball made of flour so fast…

00:17:44.823 --> 00:17:47.459
…but they didn't even go near
Saburoumaru-san's corpse.

00:17:48.226 --> 00:17:51.063
That's when I realized that Saburoumaru-san
was actually alive.

00:17:52.531 --> 00:17:56.001
And then, hint number four. The handkerchief
that was on the floor.

00:17:59.604 --> 00:18:01.440
Oh! That's mine!

00:18:01.573 --> 00:18:03.341
So it is yours!

00:18:03.775 --> 00:18:08.847
You're the only person who would have a
handkerchief with the Tokyo U emblem on it.

00:18:09.014 --> 00:18:11.349
It's none of your business! That's my favorite one!

00:18:11.883 --> 00:18:14.186
But how was that a hint?

00:18:14.786 --> 00:18:17.355
He might have dropped it before he got murdered.

00:18:17.923 --> 00:18:20.058
My nose is as keen as that of a dog's.

00:18:21.059 --> 00:18:23.895
The same cologne scent that
is on this handkerchief…

00:18:24.329 --> 00:18:26.932
…was also hanging in the air at
Gouda-san's murder scene.

00:18:28.166 --> 00:18:32.437
So that's why I thought that Saburoumaru-san
might still be alive.

00:18:32.738 --> 00:18:33.572
Give it back!

00:18:34.372 --> 00:18:38.610
And the last conclusive piece of evidence that made
us think that the culprit is Dan Sensei was…

00:18:39.244 --> 00:18:41.513
Hint number five. The positions bf the portraits.

00:18:44.116 --> 00:18:47.018
Those portraits were too low for Kinta to see easily.

00:18:47.319 --> 00:18:50.756
But they were displayed at the perfect
height for a grade schooler like me.

00:18:51.656 --> 00:18:55.193
In other words, they were displayed on the
wall lower than they normally should be.

00:18:56.094 --> 00:18:59.898
That was because they had to be lowered
a certain height for you, Dan-Sensei.

00:19:00.699 --> 00:19:03.602
So you could reach them from your
wheelchair. Isn't That right?

00:19:04.302 --> 00:19:05.303
That's correct.

00:19:05.937 --> 00:19:07.072
Good job noticing it.

00:19:09.441 --> 00:19:16.014
But why did the members of Class A
have to do this for us in Class Q?

00:19:16.248 --> 00:19:18.917
We're the ones who really want to know that.

00:19:21.052 --> 00:19:24.923
Why did you make us do things like this, Sensei?

00:19:25.423 --> 00:19:31.596
Seriously. Why did we have to come all this way just
to trick and provoke the students of Class Q?

00:19:31.997 --> 00:19:32.964
Provoke?

00:19:33.465 --> 00:19:34.833
Hey, Dan-Sensei.

00:19:35.300 --> 00:19:39.805
You didn't bring us dropouts all the way here just
so that you could play a joke on us, did you?

00:19:40.539 --> 00:19:43.074
You guys are not dropouts.

00:19:44.576 --> 00:19:47.979
There's a hidden meaning to Class Q's letter Q.

00:19:48.513 --> 00:19:50.148
Hidden meaning?

00:19:50.816 --> 00:19:51.950
Is it the Qin Quiz?

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:53.652
Or can it be Qin Ambulance (Kyukyusha)?

00:19:56.121 --> 00:19:57.823
Q's true meaning is…

00:19:58.857 --> 00:19:59.691
Qualified.

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:04.396
Meaning you meet the requirements.

00:20:06.231 --> 00:20:07.532
In other words, Class Q are…

00:20:08.233 --> 00:20:14.439
…the candidates qualified to succeed me as the
Tokyo Police's specially certified detective.

00:20:16.441 --> 00:20:17.342
No way…

00:20:17.642 --> 00:20:18.577
We are…

00:20:19.177 --> 00:20:21.213
Dan-sensei's SUCCESSORS?

00:20:21.847 --> 00:20:29.988
This training camp was your last examination
to see if you were really suited for Class Q.

00:20:30.355 --> 00:20:31.189
How could that be?

00:20:31.723 --> 00:20:35.961
Are you saying that the competent seniors at DDS

00:20:36.061 --> 00:20:40.699
…and we who have been believing that we are
at the top don't have that qualification?

00:20:41.199 --> 00:20:43.201
No, I'm not saying that.

00:20:43.668 --> 00:20:47.572
There are a lot of students at DDS for
whom I have high expectations.

00:20:48.473 --> 00:20:50.709
Also, in this training camp…

00:20:51.176 --> 00:20:53.578
If I had seen somebody who disappointed
my expectations…

00:20:54.145 --> 00:20:57.549
I would have replaced that person
with one of you Class A students.

00:20:58.049 --> 00:20:59.584
And I intend to do just the same from now on.

00:21:00.185 --> 00:21:04.623
Their total strength will still probably
fall behind you guys.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:10.295
But I want my successor to have not
just an excellent reasoning ability.

00:21:10.795 --> 00:21:14.532
But also a strong feeling of justice
and courage that would…

00:21:14.799 --> 00:21:17.202
…make them go up against difficult
situations without flinching.

00:21:21.106 --> 00:21:25.143
And that's just what Class Q showed this time
as they went against the cruel murders…

00:21:25.543 --> 00:21:29.648
…that were happening here and
solved the mystery of the case.

00:21:32.017 --> 00:21:34.119
That badge suits you well.

00:21:35.553 --> 00:21:38.089
I will now officially announce,
as the headmaster of DDS

00:21:38.523 --> 00:21:41.092
The members of Class Q.

00:21:42.494 --> 00:21:43.595
The first one is…

00:21:44.329 --> 00:21:44.930
Kyuu-kun.

00:21:44.930 --> 00:21:46.298
Yes!

00:21:46.298 --> 00:21:47.532
Narusawa Kazuma-kun.

00:21:47.532 --> 00:21:49.067
Yes!

00:21:49.067 --> 00:21:50.302
Minami Megumi-kun.

00:21:50.302 --> 00:21:52.037
Yes.

00:21:52.037 --> 00:21:53.471
Touyama Kintarou-kun.

00:21:53.471 --> 00:21:55.006
Yes!

00:21:55.006 --> 00:21:57.442
And as a new member…

00:21:58.076 --> 00:21:59.144
Amakusa Ryuu-kun.

00:22:03.048 --> 00:22:07.485
He's a student who was accepted after taking the
entrance exam in New York where he was studying.

00:22:08.420 --> 00:22:11.923
I will be teaching him personally
just like you guys from now on.

00:22:12.924 --> 00:22:15.994
Oh, is that so! Ryuu-kun's a member
of Class Q, too, now!

00:22:16.695 --> 00:22:17.162
Let's do our best!

00:22:17.696 --> 00:22:19.264
Yeah, same to you, too.

00:22:19.631 --> 00:22:20.732
Fellow detectives.

00:22:21.633 --> 00:22:25.670
You all have just began on the starting
line as members of Class Q.

00:22:27.005 --> 00:22:28.907
I wish you the best of luck from now on.

00:22:28.907 --> 00:22:33.478
Yay!

00:22:33.478 --> 00:22:34.579
Alright!

00:22:35.080 --> 00:22:36.581
Woohoo!

00:22:58.670 --> 00:23:02.640
Seriously, you came up with such a troublesome
training camp, Dan-Sensei.

00:23:03.141 --> 00:23:07.779
Exactly. We had to reconstruct the island's
facilities. It was troublesome.

00:23:08.513 --> 00:23:11.116
I even injured myself.

00:23:13.318 --> 00:23:14.652
Sorry. Sorry.

00:23:15.353 --> 00:23:21.493
But one of those five may become
my successor someday.

00:23:22.694 --> 00:23:27.499
I intend to give them all I have
to offer as a detective.

00:23:28.099 --> 00:23:32.303
As my, Dan Morihiko's, last task.

00:23:36.640 --> 00:23:47.570
Unable to cry in front of you, I'm whistling instead.

00:23:50.280 --> 00:24:02.130
Saying "I'll always be beside you" without saying a single word.

00:24:02.130 --> 00:24:09.220
My loving heart is overflowing; those sad thoughts...

00:24:09.220 --> 00:24:14.850
are like things that fade away unnoticed in mid-air.

00:24:15.050 --> 00:24:21.060
And again, with a mighty smile of relief...

00:24:21.190 --> 00:24:26.610
I will see you off.

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:36.450
Goodbye and thank you.

00:24:37.336 --> 00:24:39.137
A mother's will is delivered by a spirit.

00:24:39.538 --> 00:24:43.942
A mysterious medium claims that she will recall the
spirit to find out where the will is concealed.

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:47.679
In order to find the truth, we attend a seance…

00:24:47.946 --> 00:24:49.915
…where an impossible murder is committed.

00:24:50.616 --> 00:24:52.818
Was it really the work of the spirit?

00:24:53.752 --> 00:24:54.820
There's only one answer!

00:24:57.155 --> 00:25:01.994
I told you that this arm was that of the supposedly
dead Saburoumaru-san, but in actuality…

00:25:02.494 --> 00:25:04.496
Why does a Tokyo University student like me…

00:25:06.465 --> 00:25:07.299
The hand!

00:25:09.701 --> 00:25:10.502
It got pulled back!
